<form version="1.1">
  <label>Kong Proxy - Service Health Overview</label>
  <description>Golden signals for vault-svc and admin-api, with Kong-vs-upstream error attribution. Start here during an incident. Every panel is built on the `kong_base` macro.</description>

  <!-- Inputs use static choices, not population searches.
       A populated dropdown costs a full `kong_base` scan over the selected
       time range on every page load - for a topology of two services and four
       routes that is a lot of I/O to render six words. It also hides a route
       that has gone silent, which is exactly the route you would be looking
       for. Static choices are free and always complete.
       Adding a route to Kong? Add one <choice> line here. -->
  <fieldset submitButton="false" autoRun="true">
    <input type="time" token="tr">
      <label>Time range</label>
      <default>
        <earliest>-4h@h</earliest>
        <latest>now</latest>
      </default>
    </input>
    <input type="dropdown" token="svc" searchWhenChanged="true">
      <label>Service</label>
      <choice value="*">All services</choice>
      <choice value="vault-svc">vault-svc</choice>
      <choice value="admin-api">admin-api</choice>
      <choice value="(no-service)">(no service matched)</choice>
      <default>*</default>
      <initialValue>*</initialValue>
      <prefix>service="</prefix>
      <suffix>"</suffix>
    </input>
    <input type="dropdown" token="rt" searchWhenChanged="true">
      <label>Route</label>
      <choice value="*">All routes</choice>
      <choice value="auth-route">auth-route</choice>
      <choice value="generic-route">generic-route</choice>
      <choice value="ee-smp-functests">ee-smp-functests</choice>
      <choice value="admin-route">admin-route</choice>
      <choice value="(no-route-matched)">(no route matched)</choice>
      <default>*</default>
      <initialValue>*</initialValue>
      <prefix>route="</prefix>
      <suffix>"</suffix>
    </input>
  </fieldset>

  <!-- ================= Row 1: headline tiles ================= -->
  <row>
    <panel>
      <title>Requests</title>
      <single>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$ | stats count</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">none</option>
        <option name="numberPrecision">0</option>
      </single>
    </panel>

    <panel>
      <title>Success rate (status &lt; 400)</title>
      <single>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| stats count as total, sum(eval(if(status&lt;400,1,0))) as ok
| eval pct=if(total&gt;0, round(ok*100/total,2), 100)
| fields pct</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">none</option>
        <option name="unit">%</option>
        <option name="numberPrecision">0.00</option>
        <option name="useColors">1</option>
        <option name="rangeColors">["0xd41f1f","0xd94e17","0xcba700","0x118832"]</option>
        <option name="rangeValues">[95,99,99.5]</option>
      </single>
    </panel>

    <panel>
      <title>5xx rate</title>
      <single>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| stats count as total, sum(eval(if(status&gt;=500,1,0))) as bad
| eval pct=if(total&gt;0, round(bad*100/total,2), 0)
| fields pct</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">none</option>
        <option name="unit">%</option>
        <option name="numberPrecision">0.00</option>
        <option name="useColors">1</option>
        <option name="rangeColors">["0x118832","0xcba700","0xd94e17","0xd41f1f"]</option>
        <option name="rangeValues">[0.5,2,5]</option>
      </single>
    </panel>

    <panel>
      <title>Short-circuited (never reached upstream)</title>
      <single>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| stats count as total, sum(short_circuited) as sc
| eval pct=if(total&gt;0, round(sc*100/total,2), 0)
| fields pct</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">none</option>
        <option name="unit">%</option>
        <option name="numberPrecision">0.00</option>
        <option name="useColors">1</option>
        <option name="rangeColors">["0x118832","0xcba700","0xd94e17","0xd41f1f"]</option>
        <option name="rangeValues">[1,5,15]</option>
      </single>
    </panel>

    <panel>
      <title>Upstream p95 latency</title>
      <single>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_proxied` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| stats p95(proxy_ms) as p95 | eval p95=round(p95,0)</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">none</option>
        <option name="unit">ms</option>
        <option name="numberPrecision">0</option>
        <option name="useColors">1</option>
        <option name="rangeColors">["0x118832","0xcba700","0xd94e17","0xd41f1f"]</option>
        <option name="rangeValues">[500,2000,10000]</option>
      </single>
    </panel>
  </row>

  <!-- ================= Row 2: error attribution ================= -->
  <row>
    <panel>
      <title>Error attribution over time - is it Kong or the upstream?</title>
      <html>
        <p>
          <b>kong</b> = Kong produced the error itself (short-circuited before the upstream, or rewrote an upstream success into an error).
          <b>upstream</b> = the upstream service returned the error and Kong passed it through.
          This is the first question to answer in any gateway incident.
        </p>
      </html>
      <chart>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| where error_source!="ok"
| timechart minspan=1m count by error_source</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="charting.chart">column</option>
        <option name="charting.chart.stackMode">stacked</option>
        <option name="charting.legend.placement">right</option>
        <option name="charting.axisTitleY.text">Errors</option>
        <option name="charting.fieldColors">{"kong":"0xd41f1f","upstream":"0xf58f39","unknown":"0x888888"}</option>
        <option name="height">300</option>
      </chart>
    </panel>

    <panel>
      <title>Error split</title>
      <chart>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| where error_source!="ok"
| stats count by error_source | sort - count</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="charting.chart">pie</option>
        <option name="charting.fieldColors">{"kong":"0xd41f1f","upstream":"0xf58f39","unknown":"0x888888"}</option>
        <option name="height">300</option>
      </chart>
    </panel>
  </row>

  <!-- ================= Row 3: the service/route matrix ================= -->
  <row>
    <panel>
      <title>Service and route health matrix</title>
      <table>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| stats count as requests,
        sum(eval(if(status&lt;400,1,0)))      as ok,
        sum(eval(if(status&gt;=400 AND status&lt;500,1,0))) as c4xx,
        sum(eval(if(status&gt;=500,1,0)))     as c5xx,
        sum(eval(if(error_source=="kong" AND status&gt;=400,1,0)))     as err_kong,
        sum(eval(if(error_source=="upstream" AND status&gt;=400,1,0))) as err_upstream,
        sum(short_circuited) as short_circuited,
        sum(retried)         as retried,
        p95(proxy_ms)        as upstream_p95_ms,
        p95(total_ms)        as total_p95_ms
        by service, route
| eval success_pct = round(ok*100/requests, 2),
       upstream_p95_ms = round(upstream_p95_ms, 0),
       total_p95_ms    = round(total_p95_ms, 0)
| fields service, route, requests, success_pct, c4xx, c5xx, err_kong, err_upstream, short_circuited, retried, upstream_p95_ms, total_p95_ms
| sort - requests</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">cell</option>
        <option name="count">20</option>
        <format type="color" field="success_pct">
          <colorPalette type="minMidMax" maxColor="#118832" midColor="#CBA700" minColor="#D41F1F"></colorPalette>
          <scale type="minMidMax" minValue="90" midValue="99" maxValue="100"></scale>
        </format>
        <format type="color" field="c5xx">
          <colorPalette type="list">[#FFFFFF,#D41F1F]</colorPalette>
          <scale type="threshold">1</scale>
        </format>
        <format type="color" field="err_kong">
          <colorPalette type="list">[#FFFFFF,#D41F1F]</colorPalette>
          <scale type="threshold">1</scale>
        </format>
        <drilldown>
          <!-- Pass the BARE route value. The target dashboard's input carries
               <prefix>route="</prefix> and applies it on arrival - sending a
               pre-wrapped route="x" here would arrive as route="route="x"".
               |u URL-encodes, which matters for the @ in time modifiers. -->
          <link target="_blank">/app/kong_proxy_monitoring/kong_route_latency?form.rt=$row.route|u$&amp;form.svc=$row.service|u$&amp;form.tr.earliest=$tr.earliest|u$&amp;form.tr.latest=$tr.latest|u$</link>
        </drilldown>
      </table>
    </panel>
  </row>

  <!-- ================= Row 4: traffic and status ================= -->
  <row>
    <panel>
      <title>Traffic by status class</title>
      <chart>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| timechart minspan=1m count by status_class</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="charting.chart">column</option>
        <option name="charting.chart.stackMode">stacked</option>
        <option name="charting.legend.placement">right</option>
        <option name="charting.fieldColors">{"2xx":"0x118832","3xx":"0x006D9C","4xx":"0xCBA700","5xx":"0xD41F1F","unknown":"0x888888"}</option>
        <option name="charting.axisTitleY.text">Requests</option>
      </chart>
    </panel>

    <panel>
      <title>Upstream targets in rotation</title>
      <html>
        <p>A step down in distinct targets means a pod left the load-balancer pool - scaled down, failed its health check, or crashed. A drop to one target is a single point of failure.</p>
      </html>
      <chart>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_proxied` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| where isnotnull(upstream_ip)
| timechart minspan=1m dc(upstream_ip) as targets</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="charting.chart">line</option>
        <option name="charting.chart.nullValueMode">connect</option>
        <option name="charting.axisTitleY.text">Distinct targets</option>
        <option name="charting.legend.placement">none</option>
      </chart>
    </panel>
  </row>

  <!-- ================= Row 5: top errors ================= -->
  <row>
    <panel>
      <title>Top failing paths (4xx and 5xx)</title>
      <table>
        <search>
          <query>`kong_base` | search $svc$ | search $rt$
| where status&gt;=400
| stats count as errors,
        values(status) as codes,
        sum(eval(if(error_source=="kong",1,0)))     as by_kong,
        sum(eval(if(error_source=="upstream",1,0))) as by_upstream
        by service, route, upstream_path
| sort - errors | head 25</query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">none</option>
        <option name="count">25</option>
      </table>
    </panel>
  </row>
</form>
